From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:15:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: answer the readiness query with prepare's
 criterion

The readiness query answered "ready" for any drainable busy state, since
prepare drains work in flight. A drainable state with no job in device
test is not drained by anything: on J71t with the GPU parked and no
client in the driver, /sys/power/suspend_ready read "ready" while every
attempt drained for 1 s and refused.

A drainable state now counts as in flight only while an accepted job is
not yet signalled (r8_queued); otherwise the query refuses it as
"busy/<reasons>", as prepare's state check will after its drain. Prepare
itself is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
index e06b48430..40cf32e4f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
@@ -442,8 +442,11 @@ static __printf(3, 4) int g5p_sleep_why(struct g5p_drm *d, int ret,
  * draining firmware events. Accepted or in-flight work is not a refusal,
  * since prepare drains it, except under the never-park envelope, where the
  * drained firmware still cannot certify. A busy state no drain clears
- * (G5P_SB_STATIC) refuses here exactly as prepare would,
- * so "ready" is never answered for it. Register samples are taken only
+ * (G5P_SB_STATIC) refuses here exactly as prepare would, and so does a
+ * drainable one with no job in flight (r8_queued: accepted, not yet
+ * signalled) to retire it: prepare's drain would wait 1 s on it and refuse.
+ * So "ready" is never answered for either. A close item still queued with
+ * no job may answer busy for a moment; prepare drains it. Register samples are taken only
  * when the GPU is already idle and the core lock is free, with the same
  * reads as g5p_sleep_certificate(); a sampled GPC 0 falls through to it.
  */
@@ -491,7 +494,8 @@ static int g5p_system_sleep_check(struct device *dev)
 	held = g5p_sleep_busy_mask(d);
 	if (held) {
 		/* Prepare drains work in flight; it cannot drain the rest. */
-		if (never_park || !g5p_sleep_busy_drains(held))
+		if (never_park || !g5p_sleep_busy_drains(held) ||
+		    !(held & BIT(G5P_SB_R8_QUEUED)))
 			ret = g5p_sleep_why(d, -EBUSY, "%s%s",
 					    never_park ? "never-park/" : "busy/",
 					    g5p_sleep_busy_list(held, list,
